==Trivia==
* This card's effect is similar to the {{TCG|Arven}} card in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], but only allows for an Item card ''or'' Pokémon Tool card to be drawn, rather than one of each.
* This card's immersive illustration includes [[Arven]], [[Juliana]], [[Nemona]], [[Penny]], {{p|Mabosstiff}}, {{p|Tarountula}}, {{p|Lechonk}}, {{p|Pawmi}}, {{p|Pawmo}}, {{p|Pawmot}}, {{p|Fuecoco}}, {{p|Nacli}}, {{p|Orthworm}}, {{p|Starly}}, {{p|Staraptor}}, {{p|Toxel}}, {{p|Persian}}, {{p|Skiddo}}, {{p|Fletchinder}}, {{p|Maschiff}}, {{p|Deerling}}, {{p|Sawsbuck}}, {{p|Psyduck}}, {{p|Surskit}}, {{p|Azurill}}, {{p|Magikarp}}, {{p|Mareep}} and {{p|Hoppip}}

===Origin===
* [[Arven]] is a student at [[Naranja Academy]]{{sup/9|S}}/[[Uva Academy]]{{sup/9|V}}. He is depicted in his Uva Academy uniform.
*This card's uncommon and super rare were first featured on {{TCG ID|Scarlet & Violet|Arven|166}} from the {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet}} expansion. The [[Poco Path]] Lighthouse, where Arven grew up as a child, is featured in the standard card's illustration.

